The '''Temple of Marimbo''' is a temple in [[Marim]], [[Ape Atoll]]; it is dedicated to the monkey goddess, [[Marimbo]]. Marimbo takes the shape of a giant gorilla, yet she is a shapeshifter. The temple is only accessible during and after [[Monkey Madness I]].

Players can use the temple for melee training without needing [[food]] or [[prayer potion]]s, being able to top up their prayer at the nearby gorilla statue. Players may use [[Dharok the Wretched's equipment|Dharok the Wretched's]] set bonus along with the use of [[Protect from Melee]] to fight the [[Monkey Guard]]s within, as they will only fight using melee. Using this method, players can keep their [[hitpoints]] at 1 to maximize damage dealt. Taking a few anti-poisons with you is recommended as the nearby level 1 [[spider]]s can poison you. The altar being so close-by also allows the player to take advantage of extra damage boosting prayers, such as [[Incredible Reflexes]], [[Ultimate Strength]], [[Chivalry]], or [[Piety]].

Since the guards occasionally heal, a single guard can award a large amount of exp whilst being relatively low effort. The bearded guards near the trapdoor will block players from moving past them, similar to [[barricade]]s in [[Castle Wars]], so it's best to avoid positioning yourself between two of them, as [[greegree]]s cannot be equipped during combat. A greegree is not required after completing [[Monkey Madness II]], but the guards will no longer be aggressive.

The [[Temple of Marimbo Dungeon]] is found under the temple, and is visited during Monkey Madness I and the [[Awowogei]] section of [[Recipe for Disaster#Awowogei|Recipe for Disaster]] quests.

